==== (2) Q(2^(1/3)), P | 5 of degree 2, y^2 = x^5-x+b^2 ====
L = Q[T]/(T0^3 - 2), #Aut(L) = 1, p = 5, decomposition (e,f) = [ <1, 1>, <1, 2> ], K = L_P = Q_(5^2)
lift "p": x -> x^5, n_tau = 2, Frobenius of K applied through the completion modulo P^13; Nmax = 12
NOTE: with e = 101 expect about 8 correct digits (evaluation loss about 2 digits); for about 9 digits use e = 108 (slower tiny integrals) or increase N
lift "q": x -> x^25, n_tau = 1, Frobenius of K applied nowhere (q-power lift); Nmax = 13
NOTE: with e = 101 expect about 4 correct digits (evaluation loss about 6 digits); for about 9 digits use e = 548 (slower tiny integrals) or increase N
W^0 = [1 0]
[0 1]
